" C " {
rngFunc ( n , mu , sig , x )
{
GetRNGstate ();
( i = 0; i < n ; i ++)
x [ i ] = rnorm ( mu , sig );
PutRNGstate ();
}
}
The function rngFunc calls the R rnorm function for generating pseudo-random numbers
from a normal distribution. Its arguments for the mean and standard deviation are passed
in as pointers to double with a pointer to double, x, being provided to store the numbers
that are generated. Note that the memory for x must be allocated in R and failure to do
so or a failure to allocate enough memory will produce unpredictable results. The actual
random numbers are generated in a for loop that is sandwiched between the requisite calls
to GetRNGstate and PutRNGstate.
The rngEx.cc code is compiled with
R CMD SHLIB rngEx . cc

